#claude
# Everything under .claude/ is local EXCEPT skills/, which are project
# assets: tests/test_audit_docs_match_cli.py asserts the existence AND
# content of .claude/skills/audit-live/SKILL.md. Ignoring the whole tree
# made those four tests unpassable on a fresh clone and in CI, while
# presenting as a missing file rather than as a packaging mistake.
# `.claude/*` (not `.claude/`) is required: git will not descend into an
# excluded DIRECTORY, so a negation inside one can never re-include it.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/rules/

# Local AI/meta docs (never ship)
memory-bank/
.github/memory-bank/
.github/copilot-instructions.md

#Panopto
panopto_models/*
PANOPTO DOWNLOADER CODE/*
cuda_libs/*

#today
today_dashboard.json

# Local dev tooling (never ship): fabricates fake sync DBs for manual testing
fake_quick_sync_setup.py
# Local health/diagnostics record (dev runs write it to the repo root;
# frozen builds write it to the per-user config dir). Never committed.
diagnostics/

# Audit runs: NEVER tracked.
#
# A run directory holds the student's real Canvas course material, a Chrome
# profile with a live logged-in session, and per-file inventories - none of it
# ours to redistribute. An earlier, finer-grained ruleset tried to keep the
# findings while excluding the material; it missed _audit_runs/_navperf/, and
# 48 real lecture PDFs and PPTX files reached the public repo as a result.
# One blanket rule cannot have that gap. Audit results live on the machine
# that produced them; the durable LESSONS belong in tests/audit/*.md.
_audit_runs/

# The WHOLE marketing register is local-only as of 2026-08-28, by the product
# owner's decision. It holds competitive analysis, draft forum replies and
# positioning notes that were previously public in a public repository.
#
# marketing/README.md states the cost of this choice in its own words: the
# folder "stops travelling between machines, which is most of its value". That
# is accepted, not overlooked. Whoever works from a second machine has to carry
# marketing/ across by hand, and nothing in git will remind them.
#
# NOT a security measure. It was checked before untracking: the folder holds no
# credentials (the only "password" match is app copy describing the OS
# credential vault), and its contents were public from 2026-08-20 to
# 2026-08-28, so anything already fetched or indexed stays fetched and indexed.
# This stops FURTHER publication; it does not retract what was published.
#
# marketing/video/ was already ignored separately from an earlier pass - two
# files GENERATED by scripts/filetype_icon_gallery.py, two video scripts.
marketing/

# UI review renders (scripts/capture_completion_gallery.py). Regenerated on
# demand and ~18 MB of PNGs.
ui-review/

# Virtualenvs. NOT ignored until 2026-08-10, changed for macOS audit.
# Ignored here rather than in a local exclude so every machine that clones this is protected.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# VS Code Remote-SSH server payload, if it ever lands inside the tree.
.vscode-server/

# The macOS Office Automation permission record (runtime state, machine-specific)
macos_permission_setup.json

#temporary
marketing/search-data*